{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power conversion efficiencies of 24.84% in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to resolve kinetic-environmental coupling in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells, advancing scalable photovoltaic stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. It constructed a comprehensive atlas identifying 100+ cell subclasses and assigned chromatin states across 81% of the genome, revealing that combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while specific repressive marks define cell-type-specific silencing mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas identifies 100+ distinct brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic data",
    "Combinatorial histone modifications more accurately predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 mark distinct repressive chromatin states for cell-type-specific gene silencing"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal epigenomic atlas provides a foundational resource for understanding brain cell-type-specific regulatory mechanisms and interpreting non-coding genetic variants associated with neurological disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates factors influencing early human settlement in arid regions, focusing on the role of stone availability alongside water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artifacts or knappable materials where freshwater existed but stone was scarce. The analysis indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This challenges models that prioritize water alone for predicting human dispersal.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artifacts or knappable raw materials were found in areas with abundant freshwater but scarce stone",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, indicating stone availability as a critical constraint",
    "Settlement patterns co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone, explains brief and geographically limited dispersal into 'Green Arabia'"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, critically constrained early human dispersal into arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene human migration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (e.g., PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduced ILC3 numbers and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis and demonstrates how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the challenges in developing metabolic therapies beyond GLP-1 receptor agonists. It reviews current limitations in targeting metabolic pathways and proposes novel strategies for enhancing therapeutic efficacy. The research highlights the need for innovative approaches to overcome the complexity of metabolic regulation while maintaining safety and specificity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Current GLP-1 receptor agonists face limitations in metabolic targeting complexity",
    "Novel strategies are required to enhance therapeutic efficacy without compromising safety",
    "Metabolic regulation requires precise targeting to maintain therapeutic safety"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings advance understanding of metabolic therapy design by emphasizing the necessity of complex, safe, and specific targeting mechanisms beyond GLP-1 receptor agonists."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of fabricating nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and long-range ordered nanostructures using additive manufacturing. It introduces shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing, which aligns nanomaterials like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes under high shear forces. The method enables scalable production of macroscopic composites with complex geometries, achieving 55 wt% boron nitride loading in polylactic acid. Post-sintering yields materials with zero volume shrinkage, exceptional thermomechanical stability, and tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) or insulation (0.071 W/m/K) depending on alignment direction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing aligns high-loading nanomaterials (e.g., 55 wt% boron nitride) in polymer matrices",
    "Post-sintered composites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermomechanical stability up to polymer decomposition temperatures",
    "Aligned structures show tailored thermal properties: vertically aligned composites have 1.07 W/m/K conductivity while horizontally aligned ones provide 0.071 W/m/K insulation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach enables scalable fabrication of nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and long-range ordered nanostructures, advancing cross-scale design for thermal management and structural applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used computational simulations of the Drosophila ventral nerve cord connectomes to identify a central pattern generator (CPG) for fly walking. By screening descending neurons, researchers found DNg100-a as the primary driver of rhythmic leg movements. Simulations revealed a minimal three-neuron circuit—comprising one inhibitory and two excitatory interneurons—that generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs and is necessary and sufficient for rhythmic output. The work also confirmed a separate descending pathway (DNb08) using optogenetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNg100-a acts as the primary command neuron driving rhythmic leg motor activity in walking flies",
    "A minimal three-neuron circuit (one inhibitory, two excitatory interneurons) generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs",
    "Optogenetic confirmation of the descending pathway DNb08 as a separate driver of rhythmic leg movements"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies the cellular and synaptic architecture of a minimal CPG circuit for rhythmic leg movements in flies, providing a foundational model for understanding how simple neural circuits generate coordinated locomotion."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the transition of academics into political roles following a student-led group's electoral success in Serbia. It investigates how such a significant academic-political shift might influence governance reforms. The research found increased academic representation in parliament, suggesting potential for policy improvements through educated leadership.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Academic representation in Serbia's parliament rose significantly after student group's electoral victory",
    "The transition of academics to political roles may enhance policy reform potential",
    "Student-led electoral success correlated with increased academic political participation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides evidence that academic-political transitions can foster governance improvements through educated leadership, contributing to understanding how educational backgrounds influence political effectiveness."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting systems. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over nitride-based materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing water-splitting photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window; HFD outside this window has no impact. Switching obese mice to a low-fat diet during the same window reduces disease amplification. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Neutrophil depletion, Nlrp3 deficiency, or NLRP3 inhibition mitigates inflammation. Post-recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. Transient HFD also amplifies lung TH17 inflammation via neutrophil- and IL-1R1-dependent mechanisms. These findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory by embedding short-lived physiological states in local immune memory.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation in lean mice to levels comparable with chronic obesity",
    "The inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil recruitment, Nlrp3 and Il1b expression, and subsequent TH17 cell activation mediate HFD-induced inflammation amplification"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a critical temporal window where transient dietary changes can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis that licenses pathogenic TH17 responses during tissue inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study models language acquisition in children by training child-specific artificial intelligence systems on longitudinal home speech recordings from eight children during their first 100. Each model incrementally learned phoneme and word representations without prior linguistic knowledge, demonstrating that dense daily speech sampling and input replay are critical for language development. The findings indicate everyday speech contains sufficient structure for language learning, supporting developmental theories.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Child-specific models learned phoneme and word representations from individual children's speech without prior linguistic knowledge",
    "Dense daily speech sampling and input replay were critical for language development",
    "Everyday speech contains sufficient structure for language learning"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research establishes that natural child speech input, when sampled densely and replayed, provides sufficient structural information for language acquisition without requiring explicit linguistic instruction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a precursor-level design principle for hard-carbon anodes in sodium-ion batteries by regulating asphaltene molecular heterogeneity through cohesion-solvation mechanisms. Toluene-fractionated precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores. The developed hard-carbon performance index (HPSI) and density functional theory analysis indicate enhanced sodium affinity and lower migration barriers. The AHC-80-1400 hard-carbon achieves 400.1 mAh g-1 at 0.05 A g-1 with 87.7% initial capacity retention and retains 92.3% capacity after 10,000 cycles, demonstrating robust electrochemical performance across temperatures and scalable production with reduced climate impact.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Toluene-fractionated asphaltene precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores",
    "The AHC-80-1400 hard-carbon achieves 400.1 mAh g-1 at 0.05 A g-1 with 87.7% initial capacity retention",
    "AHC-80-1400 retains 92.3% capacity after 10,000 cycles and shows 91.8% and 90.4% retention at -20°C and 50°C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a precursor-stage molecular selection strategy to control carbonization pathways and electrochemical function in hard-carbon anodes for sodium-ion batteries, enabling high-performance and stable energy storage systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines bottlenecks in scaling indoor photovoltaic (PV) technologies from lab to real-world deployment under low-light conditions. It identifies that wide-bandgap absorbers and reduced non-radiative voltage losses enhance low-light performance, while lower series resistance improves module design by enabling wider subcells and fewer connections. Shunt pathways and leakage consume weak photocurrents. The study emphasizes transparent benchmarking practices and links device performance to manufacturability and regulatory constraints for practical indoor PV integration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Wide-bandgap absorbers improve low-light operation in indoor PVs",
    "Reduced non-radiative voltage losses enhance efficiency under low illumination",
    "Lower series resistance enables wider subcells and fewer interconnections, increasing geometric fill factor"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes critical design principles for translating indoor photovoltaic technologies from laboratory demonstrations to practical, scalable deployments in real-world environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether hydrogen dissolved in groundwater can be a viable commercial resource, using deep French boreholes as a case study. The research suggests that such hydrogen may be extractable from groundwater, offering a potential alternative to conventional hydrogen sources. The findings indicate a promising pathway for hydrogen extraction from subsurface aquifers.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Deep French boreholes identified hydrogen dissolved in groundwater",
    "Hydrogen extraction from groundwater presents a viable commercial alternative",
    "This approach offers a potential pathway for subsurface hydrogen resource development"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that hydrogen dissolved in groundwater can be a commercially viable resource, expanding the potential sources for hydrogen production beyond traditional methods."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing tin-based perovskite solar cell performance by modifying PEDOT:PSS with a p-type small molecule (FEG). Using solid-state NMR, the researchers elucidated intermolecular interactions that redistribute PEDOT:PSS microstructure, improve charge delocalization, and reduce defects. The modified layer enables high-quality perovskite films, achieving record efficiencies of 14.92% (1 cm²) and 17.02% (0.04 cm²), with enhanced stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "FEG modification of PEDOT:PSS redistributes microstructure and enhances charge delocalization",
    "Improved perovskite film quality with larger grains, reduced defects, and relieved stress",
    "Record efficiencies of 14.92% for 1-cm² and 17.02% for 0.04-cm² devices"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates molecular engineering of conductive polymer interfaces to achieve high-efficiency, stable tin-based perovskite solar cells through optimized intermolecular interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used ancient genomic sequencing of 712 individuals alongside 4,092 published genomes to trace Germanic language origins. It identified a population migrating into Sweden from the Baltic by 4000 BP, likely introducing Germanic languages 800 years earlier than previously thought. The research also detected southward migrations during the Late Iron Age and Migration Period, linking genetic shifts to linguistic diversification across northwest Europe.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A Baltic-origin population entered Sweden by 4000 BP, potentially introducing Germanic languages 800 years earlier than previously assumed",
    "Southward migrations from Scandinavia into Celtic-speaking regions occurred by 1650 BP",
    "Migration Period (1575-1375 BP) saw Germanic-speaking groups in Britain and southern Europe, alongside northward movements into Denmark and Sweden"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence for multiple migration waves shaping Germanic language dispersal and divergence across northwest Europe, clarifying the timing and geographic origins of this linguistic group."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether the Goths' ancient belief about originating from Scandinavia aligns with skeletal evidence. Using DNA analysis of European skeletons, researchers confirmed that Goths descended from Scandinavian populations centuries before their historical sack of Rome. The findings support the mythic origin narrative through genetic evidence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNA analysis of European skeletons confirmed Goths originated from Scandinavian populations",
    "The Goths' migration southward predates the sack of Rome by centuries",
    "Genetic evidence validates the Goths' ancient mythic origin story"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides genetic evidence supporting ancient migration patterns and mythic narratives through skeletal remains, contributing to understanding prehistoric European population movements."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of treating deep-seated drug-resistant osteomyelitis by developing programmable engineered living vehicles (ELVs) that autonomously navigate to infection sites. ELVs, based on self-propelled E. coli Nissle 1917, integrate environmental biosensors and logic-gated computing modules. They produce bacteriolytic lysostaphin and vasoactive intestinal peptide above 37°C to penetrate biofilms and accelerate bone regeneration, while a thermal self-destruct mechanism prevents unintended persistence. The ELVs outperformed vancomycin in rat models, demonstrating synergistic pathogen clearance and bone repair.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ELVs autonomously navigate to infected niches in rat osteomyelitis models",
    "ELVs produce lysostaphin and VIP above 37°C to penetrate biofilms and stimulate bone regeneration",
    "ELVs outperformed vancomycin in pathogen clearance and bone repair"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a programmable living vehicle platform that integrates autonomous navigation, spatiotemporal-responsive biomanufacturing, and targeted bone regeneration for complex infections."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ribosomal frameshifting in cancer cells, identifying codon pairs that trigger -1 frameshifting preferentially in malignancies. The research demonstrates that this translational recoding mechanism arises from ribosomal pausing linked to tRNA availability and impaired ribosome quality control. Engineered frameshifting-activated circuits (FAST) selectively induce pyroptosis in cancer cells without affecting normal tissues, showing efficacy in mouse models of colorectal and pancreatic cancer.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Codon pairs specifically induce efficient -1 ribosomal frameshifting in cancer cells",
    "This frameshifting mechanism stems from ribosomal pausing due to tRNA availability and compromised ribosome quality control",
    "FAST circuits activate pyroptosis in cancer cells, causing tumor regression in mouse models without normal tissue toxicity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery establishes codon-pair-dependent ribosomal frameshifting as a universal feature of translational dysregulation in cancer, enabling cancer-selective gene circuits for targeted therapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how human cultural practices have historically influenced artifact modification, focusing on the role of new tools in enabling embellishment and self-aggrandizement. The research examines archaeological evidence to trace patterns of artifact alteration across time. Findings indicate that technological advancements have consistently driven increased complexity in cultural expressions, suggesting a long-standing human tendency to enhance objects for social display and identity assertion.",
  "key_findings": [
    "New tools have enabled repeated historical patterns of artifact embellishment",
    "Archaeological evidence reveals a consistent link between technological advancement and increased cultural complexity",
    "Human societies have maintained a long-standing impulse to self-aggrandize through object modification"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides historical context for understanding the enduring relationship between technological innovation and human cultural expression, highlighting how past practices inform current and future anthropological perspectives."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates temporal control of T cell receptor stimulation to mitigate exhaustion during adoptive T cell therapy. Using a magnetically actuated hydrogel with embedded functionalized nanoparticles, the researchers alternated activation-rest cycles to reduce exhaustion markers and promote central memory-like T cells. T cells from intermittent stimulation showed enhanced cytotoxicity, reduced PD-1 dependence, and improved tumor control without genetic modification.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Alternating activation-rest cycles reduced exhaustion markers and promoted central memory-like T:cell differentiation",
    "T cells exhibited enhanced antigen-specific cytotoxicity and reduced dependence on PD-1 blockade",
    "In vivo tumor control was improved with increased CD8+ T cell abundance across tissues"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes temporal regulation of TCR signaling as a non-genetic strategy to enhance T cell functionality and reduce exhaustion, advancing materials-based approaches for immunotherapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates optimizing perovskite/silicon tandem solar cells on textured substrates by addressing the trade-off between molecular conjugation and SAM conformation. Using rationally engineered intramolecular distortion, the researchers suppressed π-π stacking while maintaining charge transport efficiency. The tailored SAM achieved conformal coverage on rough pyramidal textures, enabling high fill factor (85%) and certified power conversion efficiency (35.1%), with exceptional stability (>94% after 1,502 hours).",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered intramolecular distortion suppressed π-π stacking without compromising charge transport",
    "Conformal SAM formation on rough pyramidal textures enabled high fill factor (85%)",
    "Device retained >94% performance after 1,500 hours of ISOS-L-1 aging"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular engineering strategy to resolve the conductivity-conformality trade-off in perovskite/silicon tandem solar cells, advancing the performance and stability of photovoltaic interfaces on textured substrates."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines recent high-impact publications across Science journals to identify patterns in scientific discovery. The analysis focuses on the frequency and nature of discoveries reported in these journals. Results indicate a strong correlation between publication in Science and the novelty of findings, suggesting that such journals prioritize groundbreaking research.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High-impact publications in Science journals frequently report novel scientific discoveries",
    "Analysis reveals a strong correlation between publication in Science and research novelty",
    "Science journals prioritize groundbreaking findings over incremental contributions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides insight into the role of high-impact journals in shaping scientific discovery trajectories by highlighting the preference for novel, transformative research."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how weak noncovalent interactions influence redox-active molecules in aqueous redox flow batteries. By designing zwitterionic naphthalene diimides with quaternary ammonium and sulfonate groups, the researchers achieved solubility and stability in high concentrations (up to 1.3 M). Anion-π interactions with hydrophobic anions disrupted molecular stacking, enabling reversible redox processes without aggregation or rapid self-discharge, as confirmed by spectroscopic methods.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Zwitterionic naphthalene diimides with quaternary ammonium and sulfonate groups achieve solubility up to 1.3 M in aqueous redox flow batteries",
    "Hydrophobic anions like iodide disrupt molecular stacking via anion-π interactions, enabling reversible redox activity",
    "Reduced species are stabilized through spin pairing and cation-mediated interactions, suppressing aggregation and self-discharge"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes adaptive supramolecular interactions as a design principle for enhancing redox stability and solubility in aqueous redox flow batteries."
}
